id: pm-631t9p
title: "Harness-detection specs inherit the ambient harness, so four tests fail under Claude Code and pass in CI on the same commit: the local verdict depends on which agent ran it"
description: "Four specs set one harness signal without clearing others; the detector prefers claude-code, so a pristine tree is red locally under Claude Code and green on runners that carry no harness variables."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 1
tags[6]: ci,harness-detection,hermeticity,local-hosted-parity,pm-cli,testing
created_at: "2026-07-31T06:27:13.527Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-31T06:28:28.432Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 150
acceptance_criteria: "Harness-detection specs clear every environment key named in the detector registry before setting the keys under test, with the clear-list derived from the registry rather than hardcoded; The suite produces identical results under at least two synthetic harness environments, asserted by running it twice in CI rather than by inspection; A gate detects specs that read an environment variable they did not set, so a newly registered harness cannot reintroduce the hazard; The hosted pipeline exercises at least one non-empty harness environment, so this class stops being invisible to CI"
value: "Makes the local gate agent-independent, which is the precondition for a multi-harness fleet trusting it at all."
impact: Agents under one harness see a pristine checkout as broken; the published green CI signal is produced by an environment no contributor uses.
why_now: A fleet of agents across several harnesses runs this gate first on every task; today it returns a different answer per agent and the hosted gate cannot see the difference.
parent: pm-u9d0
risk: medium
confidence: high
severity: high
environment: "HEAD at 2026.7.31, Linux, node scripts/run-tests.mjs test, ambient CLAUDECODE=1"
repro_steps: node scripts/run-tests.mjs test  => 4 failed / 6579 passed; then env -u CLAUDECODE -u CLAUDE_CODE -u CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID -u CLAUDE_CODE_ENTRYPOINT node scripts/run-tests.mjs test -- tests/unit/core/shared/shared-helpers.spec.ts tests/unit/commands/claim-command.spec.ts tests/unit/sdk/agent-runtime-primitives.spec.ts  => 65 passed
expected_result: The test verdict for a commit is identical regardless of which harness runs the suite.
actual_result: "Four harness-detection specs fail under Claude Code and pass under codex and on bare CI runners, on the same commit with no source changes."
component: tests/harness-detection
